WEBVTT

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:28.445
Planet Express crew,
report to headquarters immediately!

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:31.240
Repeat, what I just said, immediately!

00:00:35.661 --> 00:00:37.037
- Sorry, Randy.
- Ah!

00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:39.540
Step away from the car,
and no one gets hurt!

00:00:43.335 --> 00:00:45.003
To the employment cave!

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:47.840
Oh.

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:53.428
Thanks, dear. Off to work.

00:01:00.686 --> 00:01:03.146
Hya! Hya!

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:04.940
Whoa, whoa, there, girl.

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:07.109
Go on, now! Get on back to Paraguay!

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.368
We're being eaten by a giant spider!

00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:17.744
There's no time for that!

00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:19.454
The Professor needs us!

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:38.432
Uh, crew, as you know, I've delivered
a lot of good news in the past.

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:42.477
But what I'm about to lay down
is by far the greatest announcement

00:01:42.561 --> 00:01:44.897
in the history of Planet Express!

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.775
What is it? I'm on the edge of my butt.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:53.071
Ladies and gentlemen,
feast your eyes on our amazing new

00:01:53.739 --> 00:01:54.907
soda machine!

00:01:56.408 --> 00:01:59.161
That's what I'm talking about!

00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:01.914
You undersold it, Professor!

00:02:02.247 --> 00:02:05.876
Look, it has Slurm Loco!
It's the extreme-iest!

00:02:06.502 --> 00:02:07.961
Hey, what can I get y'all?

00:02:08.045 --> 00:02:11.507
Wow, you can talk?
Shut up and give me a Slurm Loco.

00:02:16.512 --> 00:02:17.513
Ooh! Ooh!

00:02:17.596 --> 00:02:20.557
Hey, drink machine,
what kind of alcoholic sodas you got?

00:02:20.766 --> 00:02:23.560
Y'all can't drink at work!
This ain't a sawmill!

00:02:23.727 --> 00:02:25.646
No alcohol? Pfft.

00:02:25.729 --> 00:02:28.440
And you got the nerve
to call yourself a beverage machine?

00:02:28.607 --> 00:02:30.442
I call myself Bev.

00:02:30.651 --> 00:02:33.070
And if you're looking
for a smelly old can of booze,

00:02:33.237 --> 00:02:34.279
go look in the mirror.

00:02:34.488 --> 00:02:36.198
- Oh, snap.
- Oh!

00:02:36.323 --> 00:02:38.659
No, no, everybody calm down.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.577
Yeah, I need one more Slurm.

00:02:45.457 --> 00:02:48.001
And one more to wash that
Slurm taste out of my mouth.

00:02:54.091 --> 00:02:56.969
So I went to the bathroom,
and my pee was green. Pretty neat, huh?

00:02:57.052 --> 00:02:59.179
I was wondering
who Shrekked in the toilet.

00:02:59.805 --> 00:03:02.391
I hope you're proud of yourself, Bev.

00:03:02.474 --> 00:03:05.519
You've turned this perfectly
worthless loser into an addict.

00:03:05.602 --> 00:03:07.271
Cut me some slack, preacher.

00:03:07.354 --> 00:03:10.232
I'm just a coal grinder's daughter
trying to stay off the pole.

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:14.027
With that big old caboose,
it'd have to be a telephone pole!

00:03:14.111 --> 00:03:15.487
Hey-o!

00:03:16.697 --> 00:03:18.740
Well, I guess a fellow's got to talk big

00:03:18.824 --> 00:03:21.493
when he's sporting a little
shriveled up antenna like that.

00:03:21.577 --> 00:03:22.995
What? You...

00:03:23.078 --> 00:03:27.124
For your information, "Madam,"
it's a grower, not a shower!

00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:34.923
My antenna's fine. It's just fine.

00:03:35.007 --> 00:03:36.925
Ladies can't get enough Bender.

00:03:37.009 --> 00:03:39.678
I need to loosen up.
Give me a screwdriver.

00:03:40.762 --> 00:03:43.265
Hello. Who's your hot, dumb friend?

00:03:43.348 --> 00:03:44.558
- Me?
- Me?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.101
Sure, why not.

00:03:54.401 --> 00:03:56.403
Hang on. It's too bright in here.

00:03:56.486 --> 00:04:00.199
Call me old-fashioned,
but I like a little romance in an orgy.

00:04:00.282 --> 00:04:02.451
Let me switch off this weird light.

00:04:02.826 --> 00:04:03.827
Ow!

00:04:04.161 --> 00:04:05.913
Fry, it's 2:00 a.m.

00:04:05.996 --> 00:04:08.290
What are you doing here
glowing on my skanks?

00:04:08.624 --> 00:04:10.626
Just sitting here
turning quarters into urine.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:15.380
We don't got to put up with this.
We got Poli Sci degrees.

00:04:15.464 --> 00:04:16.924
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Hang on.

00:04:17.007 --> 00:04:18.926
I'll just politely escort him
to the gutter.

00:04:19.551 --> 00:04:20.886
Scram, shiny!

00:04:21.762 --> 00:04:23.222
All right, how we feeling?

00:04:23.305 --> 00:04:26.225
Hot. I could bake a potato in my cleavage.

00:04:26.308 --> 00:04:28.310
Yeah, I need a seltzer.

00:04:29.978 --> 00:04:32.231
I'd be honored
to purchase you some refreshment.

00:04:32.414 --> 00:04:36.460
Uh, hey, drink machine, you got anything
classy for these delicate flowers?

00:04:36.543 --> 00:04:39.755
I ain't making drinks
for no trashy robo-sluts.

00:04:39.838 --> 00:04:43.300
Trashy? At least
I don't put out for quarters.

00:04:46.803 --> 00:04:48.930
Hey!

00:04:49.014 --> 00:04:51.975
Hey. Stop that, drink machine.

00:04:52.059 --> 00:04:53.352
Stop it, I say.

00:04:53.977 --> 00:04:55.938
That's it, we're out of here.

00:04:56.063 --> 00:04:57.689
Come on. We'll split a blintz.

00:04:57.773 --> 00:05:00.025
Wait, give me a chance
to defend your honor

00:05:00.108 --> 00:05:01.693
and then sully it on the couch.

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:07.324
All right, I've been waiting all day
for an excuse to hit a lady.

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:09.826
You try it, and I'll bash your face in.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.830
Ooh! I'm so scared, No-Arms.

00:05:20.212 --> 00:05:22.172
You want some of this?

00:05:31.348 --> 00:05:32.724
- Interesting.
- Mmm!

00:05:36.294 --> 00:05:40.465
Uh, Fry? You're glowing like
the Human Torch on prom night.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:44.077
Shouldn't you be standing on a rocky coast
somewhere preventing shipwrecks?

00:05:46.238 --> 00:05:49.366
Nice, hate me
because of the brightness of my skin.

00:05:54.037 --> 00:05:56.331
You okay, ma'am?
I think your soda water broke.

00:06:01.753 --> 00:06:04.840
My God! Bev just had a baby in my cup!

00:06:07.843 --> 00:06:09.511
I know, right?

00:06:09.594 --> 00:06:10.679
I better take that.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.226
Aw. He's so cute. Wait. No, he isn't.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:17.728
He looks like Bender!

00:06:20.397 --> 00:06:24.109
Oh, no, no, no.
No way am I that kid's dad!

00:06:24.192 --> 00:06:26.570
Wipe my tiny metal ass!

00:06:27.571 --> 00:06:28.655
Ah, crap.

00:06:32.993 --> 00:06:35.162
Mama, thirsty.

00:06:35.245 --> 00:06:37.414
Hang on, dumpling. My milk's coming in.

00:06:43.211 --> 00:06:45.005
Ugh. In public?

00:06:45.088 --> 00:06:47.341
Aw, biscuits! I'm a father?

00:06:47.424 --> 00:06:48.550
How did this happen?

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:50.594
Does this ring a bell?

00:06:50.677 --> 00:06:52.804
Are you telling me
the stuff we did in private,

00:06:52.888 --> 00:06:56.642
and also twice on the sidewalk,
made a baby robot? How?

00:06:56.725 --> 00:07:00.854
Aw, Bender, didn't your mom ever tell you
where robot babies come from?

00:07:00.938 --> 00:07:03.607
No. She was a religious fundamentalist.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.985
Plus she didn't have a mouth.
It's an unusual combination.

00:07:07.069 --> 00:07:10.739
Come on, everyone,
let's take Bender to the teen center

00:07:10.822 --> 00:07:13.408
to learn about the bots and the bees!

00:07:17.371 --> 00:07:19.957
It's okay, Bender.
No one here will laugh at you

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.250
for not knowing
where robot babies come from.

00:07:25.337 --> 00:07:26.838
We don't know, either.

00:07:26.922 --> 00:07:29.174
Then prepare to be embarrassed.

00:07:33.136 --> 00:07:34.179
Or...

00:07:36.306 --> 00:07:39.351
Meet Gerald, a maturing young robot.

00:07:39.434 --> 00:07:41.478
Hey, he looks like me!

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:44.022
His hideous appearance is a by-product

00:07:44.106 --> 00:07:47.276
of his hardware gearing up
for an important mission,

00:07:47.359 --> 00:07:48.735
reproduction.

00:07:48.819 --> 00:07:50.445
Oh, boy, oh, boy, oh, boy!

00:07:50.529 --> 00:07:54.574
Since factories can't manufacture
enough robots to meet demand,

00:07:54.658 --> 00:07:57.035
robots can also reproduce by mating.

00:07:57.119 --> 00:07:58.704
Oh, now you tell me!

00:07:58.787 --> 00:08:02.040
First, Gerald must find a female robot.

00:08:02.124 --> 00:08:04.668
The best he can do is Francine.

00:08:05.919 --> 00:08:08.880
After beer and hot wings
at a local gas station,

00:08:08.964 --> 00:08:12.134
the two enjoy intimate time
behind a Dumpster.

00:08:12.217 --> 00:08:14.678
It's all perfectly natural.

00:08:14.761 --> 00:08:16.847
Let's watch, aroused,

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:21.893
as Gerald's antenna uploads a binary file
to Francine's internal drive.

00:08:24.354 --> 00:08:27.441
Manufacturing specs
fromeach parent are then merged

00:08:27.524 --> 00:08:29.401
by a randomized algorithm,

00:08:29.484 --> 00:08:33.196
and the resulting code
guides assembly of a new robot.

00:08:34.781 --> 00:08:38.702
Yes, everything your body does
is perfectly natural.

00:08:38.785 --> 00:08:42.164
Except masturbation. That's just wrong.

00:08:44.166 --> 00:08:45.292
Oh...

00:08:45.375 --> 00:08:47.127
I can't believe I made a kid!

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:48.503
I'm not ready!

00:08:48.587 --> 00:08:50.964
There's so much of the world
I haven't stolen yet!

00:08:51.048 --> 00:08:54.343
Relax, Bender.
No one would let you near a child.

00:08:54.426 --> 00:08:56.887
Bev will get custody,
and you'll be a deadbeat dad

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.222
who never even bothers
to know his own son.

00:08:59.306 --> 00:09:01.266
You really think so?

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.978
I know so.
You're absolutely horrible in every way.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:07.022
You're sweet, Leela.

00:09:12.319 --> 00:09:15.572
Sorry, Bev,
but I ain't cut out for fatherhood.

00:09:15.656 --> 00:09:19.409
So here's my certificate of abandonment
drawn up by our notary.

00:09:19.493 --> 00:09:20.535
That'll be 10 bucks.

00:09:20.619 --> 00:09:24.122
Now take your kid
and hit the soup line!

00:09:24.957 --> 00:09:26.792
Oh, no, you don't, mister!

00:09:26.875 --> 00:09:28.752
Damn baby's driving me crazy!

00:09:29.962 --> 00:09:33.298
He won't stop giggling
no matter how much I scream at him!

00:09:35.968 --> 00:09:37.094
There, there.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.764
I still got womanly needs!

00:09:40.889 --> 00:09:45.018
Who's gonna look twice at me with this
dirty leech hanging off my dairy nozzle?

00:09:45.102 --> 00:09:46.395
Not me, that's for sure.

00:09:46.478 --> 00:09:49.356
Then it's settled! He's all yours, Pappy!

00:09:49.439 --> 00:09:51.525
Hey, wait! You can't leave... What?

00:09:58.073 --> 00:10:00.659
Ah... Ah!

00:10:25.559 --> 00:10:27.394
What the...

00:10:27.477 --> 00:10:29.855
Can't I have
one moment to myself?

00:10:31.732 --> 00:10:33.025
Why can't you sleep?

00:10:33.108 --> 00:10:35.444
I left my window open, and moths got in.

00:10:35.527 --> 00:10:38.530
I swear, if I wasn't such a great dad,

00:10:38.614 --> 00:10:41.116
I'd grab
his ugly little neck and...

00:10:44.369 --> 00:10:46.705
Hey, he stopped screaming for a second!

00:10:46.788 --> 00:10:48.081
Bend some other stuff!

00:10:52.169 --> 00:10:53.670
Ah!

00:10:53.754 --> 00:10:54.880
Bend! Bend!

00:10:54.963 --> 00:10:57.215
He loves bending, just like me.

00:10:57.758 --> 00:11:02.262
Aw, I'm gonna call him Ben,
after the first half of me, Bender.

00:11:03.639 --> 00:11:05.057
That's my bastard.

00:11:29.081 --> 00:11:30.499
Whoo-hoo!

00:11:37.005 --> 00:11:40.092
Bend it, Daddy!
Bend it like it called you poo-poo-face!

00:11:40.175 --> 00:11:41.301
It called me what?

00:11:44.096 --> 00:11:46.306
Yay! You bended it like a pretzel.

00:11:48.016 --> 00:11:49.810
Okay, now you.

00:11:54.856 --> 00:11:56.692
I can't do it!

00:11:56.775 --> 00:11:59.736
Hey, buddy, you're learning.
You'll get there.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.113
Bender, I was wrong.

00:12:01.196 --> 00:12:03.240
You're a fine parent, and I want to...

00:12:03.323 --> 00:12:04.950
- Leela was wrong!
- Leela was wrong!

00:12:05.033 --> 00:12:06.660
- Leela was wrong!
- Leela was wrong!

00:12:08.996 --> 00:12:11.415
Daddy, how'd you get so good at bending?

00:12:11.498 --> 00:12:14.584
I inherited my arm control software
from my mom.

00:12:14.668 --> 00:12:16.878
That's how it's passed down,
mother to son.

00:12:16.962 --> 00:12:19.548
But my mommy had no arms!

00:12:19.631 --> 00:12:22.134
Does that mean I can never be a bender?

00:12:22.217 --> 00:12:25.846
Well, sure you can! You just need
to get a bending card installed.

00:12:25.929 --> 00:12:29.725
I hate to crush a boy's dreams,
but what the heck.

00:12:29.808 --> 00:12:34.521
He has only one expansion slot,
and it holds his memory card.

00:12:34.605 --> 00:12:37.149
This robot will never bend.

00:12:37.899 --> 00:12:40.777
Don't tell my son
what he can and can't do!

00:12:40.861 --> 00:12:44.281
You may know what's in his head,
but you don't know what's in his heart!

00:12:45.407 --> 00:12:47.284
There's no slot in there, either.

00:12:47.367 --> 00:12:48.452
I said shut up!

00:12:54.583 --> 00:12:57.836
Today marks
young Ben's thirteenth day

00:12:57.919 --> 00:13:00.130
of being left on continuously.

00:13:00.213 --> 00:13:04.426
And so, before the Lord
and this congregation,

00:13:04.509 --> 00:13:09.431
we upgrade him to man-bot.
Can I get a mazel tov?

00:13:09.514 --> 00:13:10.891
Mazel tov!

00:13:10.974 --> 00:13:12.017
Mazel tov!

00:13:12.517 --> 00:13:15.228
I'd like to thank
the preacher-bot for the introduction

00:13:15.312 --> 00:13:18.482
and also for not circumcising
me again, am I right?

00:13:20.067 --> 00:13:25.113
Twice was enough. But seriously,
today, I'm not just a man-bot,

00:13:25.197 --> 00:13:27.616
I'm the luckiest man-bot alive.

00:13:27.699 --> 00:13:29.868
My mom may have abandoned me,

00:13:29.952 --> 00:13:32.746
but I have the greatest dad
in the whole universe.

00:13:33.538 --> 00:13:37.125
He's patient,
he's not afraid to show his emotions...

00:13:37.209 --> 00:13:38.293
Don't look at me!

00:13:38.377 --> 00:13:41.129
...and someday, if my dreams come true,

00:13:41.213 --> 00:13:43.090
I'll be a bender, just like him.

00:13:44.007 --> 00:13:45.968
You must be so proud of your boy.

00:13:46.093 --> 00:13:48.261
I could take him or leave him.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.057
I'm back for my son!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:54.685
I've come to take him and leave with him!

00:13:55.852 --> 00:13:57.813
She beat you to both things!

00:14:03.277 --> 00:14:06.071
It's okay, Son, Mama's here now.

00:14:06.154 --> 00:14:08.323
Daddy! Don't let her take me!

00:14:08.407 --> 00:14:10.575
Get your lack of hands off my boy!

00:14:10.659 --> 00:14:13.328
You're an unfit parent
who abandoned her child!

00:14:13.412 --> 00:14:16.832
Oh, yeah?
Well, I'm still less unfitter than you.

00:14:16.915 --> 00:14:18.000
Says who?

00:14:18.083 --> 00:14:21.461
Says this document you gave me
when you tried to abandon Ben first!

00:14:24.715 --> 00:14:25.716
It's genuine.

00:14:27.301 --> 00:14:29.511
That doesn't prove I'm an unfit parent!

00:14:29.594 --> 00:14:31.555
I was drunk and violent
when I signed that!

00:14:31.638 --> 00:14:34.850
Well, I'm drunk and violent now.
He's coming with me!

00:14:35.517 --> 00:14:37.644
Daddy!

00:14:37.728 --> 00:14:40.814
Son!

00:14:44.484 --> 00:14:47.571
My boy's gone.
All I have left to remember him

00:14:47.654 --> 00:14:49.948
are these innocent playthings
we stole together.

00:14:52.242 --> 00:14:54.703
Fry, put these someplace safe.

00:14:58.832 --> 00:15:01.293
That's it, Fry!
For a guy who's not too bright,

00:15:01.376 --> 00:15:02.836
you're too damn bright!

00:15:02.919 --> 00:15:05.005
Now, get out! And don't come back

00:15:05.088 --> 00:15:08.175
until someone finds a use
for a million-watt idiot!

00:15:19.937 --> 00:15:22.314
Mom, will I ever get to see Dad again?

00:15:22.397 --> 00:15:26.068
No, he died yesterday.
Rust monsters ate his face.

00:15:26.151 --> 00:15:27.444
Sweet dreams!

00:15:35.953 --> 00:15:38.622
Psst! Quit whimpering
or you don't get kidnapped.

00:15:38.705 --> 00:15:40.123
Dad!

00:15:42.417 --> 00:15:45.087
Oh... Come on. Let's run for it.

00:15:56.014 --> 00:15:57.557
What's going to happen to us now, Dad?

00:15:57.641 --> 00:16:00.644
Well, I reckon we'll just sit around
this campfire a while.

00:16:00.727 --> 00:16:01.853
But then what?

00:16:01.937 --> 00:16:05.232
Only a fool plans
more than a few centuries ahead, Son.

00:16:07.109 --> 00:16:08.819
Freeze, tin woodsman!

00:16:08.902 --> 00:16:13.156
You're under arrest for kidnapping
and burning raccoons without a permit!

00:16:23.041 --> 00:16:24.960
- It's over, Dad.
- It ain't over!

00:16:25.043 --> 00:16:28.839
I can't outrun a hovercopter,
but I can out-bend it!

00:16:40.475 --> 00:16:42.269
I know! Let's outrun it!

00:16:46.607 --> 00:16:48.567
- There's a dam!
- Damn!

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:49.651
There's a grate!

00:16:49.735 --> 00:16:51.778
- Great!
- But I can't bend anything

00:16:51.862 --> 00:16:54.698
with my arms agonizingly maimed like this.

00:16:54.781 --> 00:16:56.074
Well, maybe I can!

00:17:01.955 --> 00:17:03.415
You can do it, Son.

00:17:13.592 --> 00:17:14.801
Yeah, this ain't gonna happen.

00:17:16.887 --> 00:17:18.263
Is that even necessary?

00:17:21.516 --> 00:17:22.768
I'm sorry, Daddy.

00:17:22.851 --> 00:17:24.728
You got nothing to be sorry about.

00:17:25.187 --> 00:17:27.189
He's really
a very good father.

00:17:28.857 --> 00:17:32.319
All right, I got her statement.
And a straight-up grape soda.

00:17:32.402 --> 00:17:34.529
Aw, yeah.

00:17:34.613 --> 00:17:36.990
I promise
things will be different, Son.

00:17:37.074 --> 00:17:39.952
From now on,
I'm chaining you to a radiator.

00:17:40.494 --> 00:17:45.040
I'm amazed someone who dispenses
such warm soda could be so coldhearted!

00:17:45.123 --> 00:17:47.584
I'm gonna buy a drink
just so I can throw it in your face!

00:17:50.754 --> 00:17:53.090
It's another soda baby!

00:17:53.173 --> 00:17:54.424
Oh...

00:17:54.967 --> 00:17:55.968
Damn.

00:17:58.887 --> 00:18:00.889
You got knocked up by a police officer

00:18:00.973 --> 00:18:03.266
while he was looking
for your kidnapped child?

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.852
Sure did! I still got it.

00:18:05.936 --> 00:18:07.104
So, now what happens?

00:18:07.187 --> 00:18:09.147
Tell you what, you keep the big one.

00:18:09.231 --> 00:18:12.484
Long as I got a baby to neglect,
I'm happy.

00:18:12.567 --> 00:18:14.194
Should we call child services?

00:18:14.278 --> 00:18:15.779
No, let's just get outta here.

00:18:19.491 --> 00:18:21.201
Whoo-hoo!

00:18:21.285 --> 00:18:23.620
Whoo! Whoo-hoo-hoo!

00:18:26.039 --> 00:18:27.040
Whoo?

00:18:27.124 --> 00:18:29.459
Sorry, Dad. I'm glad to be back.

00:18:29.543 --> 00:18:31.878
I'm just kind of bummed
I can't bend stuff.

00:18:31.962 --> 00:18:35.549
All I ever wanted was
to go to Bending State-Santa Cruz.

00:18:35.632 --> 00:18:37.134
But that's never gonna happen.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:41.430
Listen, you need something bent,
you come to me, huh, champ?

00:18:47.936 --> 00:18:50.230
Damn it, I love that little guy so much!

00:18:50.314 --> 00:18:53.900
I'd sacrifice any four of you
if it would help him bend even a little!

00:18:53.984 --> 00:18:57.863
There is one way,
but no, it's too horrible.

00:18:57.946 --> 00:19:00.198
Nothing's too horrible for my boy!

00:19:00.282 --> 00:19:03.952
Well, I could install a bending card.

00:19:04.036 --> 00:19:05.871
But you said he only has one slot!

00:19:05.954 --> 00:19:08.832
Correct. I'd have to remove
his memory card.

00:19:08.915 --> 00:19:12.044
He'd be able to bend,
but he'd lose all his memories.

00:19:12.127 --> 00:19:14.963
He wouldn't even remember who you are.

00:19:28.977 --> 00:19:30.896
You sure you want to be a bender, Son?

00:19:30.979 --> 00:19:32.481
More than anything.

00:19:34.566 --> 00:19:37.235
Just remember, your daddy loves you.

00:19:37.319 --> 00:19:40.489
Remember that, will you, Son?
Remember that.

00:19:42.157 --> 00:19:43.784
Dad, are you crying?

00:19:45.577 --> 00:19:48.747
No! I said with the mouth
you're looking at.

00:19:59.883 --> 00:20:02.678
You sure
take after your old man!

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:04.513
I never knew my father.

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.014
Ooh!

00:20:06.098 --> 00:20:07.391
It's not important.

00:20:07.474 --> 00:20:09.309
What is important is that we get you

00:20:09.393 --> 00:20:12.145
to Bending State-Santa Cruz
in time for registration.

00:20:12.229 --> 00:20:15.107
Then we'd better hurry.
Registration ends in one hour.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:16.316
To the ship!

00:20:19.653 --> 00:20:20.737
Ugh.

00:20:20.821 --> 00:20:22.155
It's too foggy.

00:20:22.239 --> 00:20:24.366
We can't navigate through this storm.

00:20:24.449 --> 00:20:25.909
Our lights aren't bright enough.

00:20:26.368 --> 00:20:27.995
I'm sorry I let you down, Son.

00:20:28.078 --> 00:20:29.079
Who are you again?

00:20:29.162 --> 00:20:32.541
It's just not possible to get you
to bending school this year.

00:20:33.083 --> 00:20:35.043
Or is there?

00:20:47.139 --> 00:20:48.807
All right, Fry!

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:52.144
Merry college registration day, everyone!